father of: Achish (H0397); also called Maacah (KJV: Maachah; NIV: Maakah) at 1Ki.2.39;
Another name of <i>ma.okh</i> (מָעוֹךְ "Maoch" H4582)
§ Maachah = "oppression"
father of Achish, king of Gath at the beginning of Solomon's reign

A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.14;
son of: Othniel (H6274)(?) whose wife was Achsah (H5915);
brother of: Hathath (H2867)(?);
father of: Ophrah (H6084I)
§ Meonothai = "my habitations"
a son of Othniel, the younger brother of Caleb

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.12.36;
son of: Jonathan (H3129K);
brother of: Zechariah (H2148Z), Shemaiah (H8098V), Azarel (H5832J), Milalai (H4450), Gilalai (H1562), Nethanel (H5417P), Judah (H3063K) and Hanani (H2607K)
§ Maai = "compassionate"
one of the sons of Asaph who took part in the musical service at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem
